🐧 Linux CLI Basics Cheat Sheet
| Goal                   | Command               | What it does                                   |
| ---------------------- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| Show current directory | `pwd`                 | Prints the working directory                   |
| List files             | `ls`                  | Lists contents                                 |
| Detailed listing       | `ls -l`               | Shows permissions, owner, size, dates, etc.    |
| Include hidden files   | `ls -al`              | Lists everything, including dotfiles           |
| Change directory       | `cd <dir>`            | Moves into a directory                         |
| Go up one level        | `cd ..`               | Moves to the parent directory                  |
| Go home                | `cd ~`                | Moves to your home directory                   |
| Find a file            | `find ~ -name <file>` | Searches your home directory                   |
| Read a file            | `cat <file>`          | Displays its contents                          |
| Current username       | `whoami`              | Shows the logged-in user                       |
| Kernel/system info     | `uname -a`            | Shows detailed kernel/system information       |
| Kernel name only       | `uname`               | Usually outputs `Linux`                        |
| Disk usage             | `df -h`               | Shows filesystem space in human-readable units |
| OS information         | `cat /etc/os-release` | Shows Linux distribution/version               |

